@startuml
title RenderConfigRepository + RenderConfigRedisMirror

allowmixing
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "serverV2/config/" {
  class RenderConfigRepository {
    - _mirror : RenderConfigRedisMirror | None
    + get() : RenderConfig
    + admin_get() : dict
    + admin_put(d: dict) : None
    - _fetch_dict() : dict
  }

  class RenderConfigRedisMirror {
    - _redis : RedisClient
    - _ttl : int = 30
    + get_cached_dict() : dict | None
    + set_cached_dict(d: dict) : None
    + invalidate() : None
  }
}

package "serverV2/infrastructure/" {
  class RedisClient
}

class RenderConfig <<dataclass>>

cloud "Firestore\n(per-env Firebase project)" as FS {
  artifact "config/global\n  .json (string)" as DOC
}

cloud "Upstash Redis\n(per-env REDIS_KEY_PREFIX)" as RD {
  artifact "<prefix>config:render\n(JSON dict, TTL=30s)" as KEY
}

RenderConfigRepository o--> RenderConfigRedisMirror : optional, ctor-injected
RenderConfigRedisMirror o--> RedisClient : ctor-injected

RenderConfigRepository ..> RenderConfig : .from_dict() builds
RenderConfigRepository ..> DOC : _fetch_dict() reads\n(only on cache miss)
RenderConfigRepository ..> DOC : admin_put() writes

RenderConfigRedisMirror ..> KEY : get / set / del

note right of RenderConfigRepository
  **get() flow**
   1. mirror.get_cached_dict()
        - hit  -> parse & return
        - miss -> step 2
   2. _fetch_dict() (Firestore)
   3. mirror.set_cached_dict(fresh)
   4. parse & return

  **admin_put() flow**
   1. Firestore write
   2. mirror.invalidate()
end note

note right of RenderConfigRedisMirror
  Fail-open: any Redis error
  (down, timeout, parse) returns
  None / silently no-ops -> repo
  falls through to Firestore.
  Never raises into the caller.
end note

note bottom of KEY
  ``namespaced("config:render")``
  -> dev:config:render
  -> staging:config:render
  -> (prod / test: empty prefix = "config:render")
  Per-env isolation when sharing Redis.
end note
@enduml
